
📘 e-Classroom Management System
📌 Project Overview
The e-Classroom Management System is a web-based application designed to facilitate online education by enabling efficient classroom management, assignment handling, attendance tracking, and notifications. The system follows modern software engineering principles and uses a scalable MVC architecture with a responsive user interface.
🏗 Application Architecture
🔹 Architectural Pattern
The application follows the Model–View–Controller (MVC) architectural pattern to ensure:
Separation of concerns
Scalability
Ease of maintenance
🔹 Components of MVC Architecture
📦 Model
The Model handles all data-related logic and database interactions.
A relational SQL database is used.
Proposed Models:
User: Stores user details such as name, role, email, and encrypted password.
Classroom: Manages classroom information including schedule and enrolled users.
Assignment: Handles assignment details and student submissions.
Attendance: Tracks attendance records for students.
🎨 View
The View is responsible for presenting data to users through a responsive UI.
Technologies Used:
React.js for frontend development
Tailwind CSS for styling
Key Features:
Dashboards
Class schedules
Assignment lists
Responsive layouts for mobile and desktop devices
🧠 Controller
The Controller acts as an intermediary between the Model and the View by:
Processing user requests
Calling appropriate model functions
Returning formatted responses to the frontend
🔹 API Development
The system uses RESTful APIs for communication between frontend and backend.
🔸 Internal APIs
User authentication
Assignment submission
Classroom management
(Using HTTP methods: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
🔸 External APIs
Nodemailer: Sends email notifications (e.g., attendance alerts)
Cloudinary: Secure cloud storage for assignments and study materials
🔹 UML Diagrams
Class Diagram: Shows relationships between User, Classroom, Assignment, and Attendance
Sequence Diagram: Illustrates assignment submission workflow
(Student → Frontend → Backend → Storage → Acknowledgment)
🗄 Data Model Schema
🔹 Entity Descriptions & Relationships
👤 User
Attributes:
userID (PK)
name
email
password (encrypted)
role (Admin, Teacher, Student)
Relationships:
One-to-many with Classroom
One-to-many with Assignment
🏫 Classroom
Attributes:
classID (PK)
className
description
teacherID (FK)
Relationships:
One-to-many with Assignment
One-to-many with Attendance
📝 Assignment
Attributes:
assignmentID (PK)
title
description
dueDate
classID (FK)
studentID (FK)
Relationships:
Many-to-one with Classroom
Many-to-one with User
📅 Attendance
Attributes:
attendanceID (PK)
date
status (Present, Absent, Tardy)
studentID (FK)
classID (FK)
🔔 Notification
Attributes:
notificationID (PK)
userID (FK)
message
status (Read/Unread)
